{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nEntering the review-bot ASGI lifespan from an ordinary test starts the real backfill reconciler and snapshot janitor, while shutdown reads the production 1200-second queue-drain default. The idiomatic `with TestClient(app)` path can therefore turn a unit test into a long-running background sweep/hang. The production default is intentional and must not change: `src/rebar/review_bot/config.py:49` defines `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS = 1200`, and `shutdown_drain_seconds()` at `src/rebar/review_bot/config.py:92` already accepts a positive `SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS` override.\n\n## Approach\nUse the existing environment knob in the root pytest harness to pin a small positive drain window for every test process. In `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py`, add one module autouse fixture that stubs `reconcile.reconcile_loop` and `rebar._snapshot.start_background_janitor` by default. A registered `real_reconcile_loop` marker will explicitly bypass only the reconciler stub for tests that exercise the real loop; the janitor remains stubbed because its filesystem sweep is unrelated to those contracts. This centralizes the exact safety setup currently duplicated around the lifespan tests at `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py:1446-1449`, `:1474-1477`, and `:1615-1618` without changing production behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/conftest.py`: register the opt-out marker and set a suite-wide bounded `SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS` default that individual tests may override.\n- `tests/unit/test_review_bot.py`: add the module autouse stubs and RED-first lifespan/escape-hatch coverage; remove duplicated per-test stubs.\n- No production files change; `src/rebar/review_bot/config.py` remains the authoritative production default and parser.\n\n## Testing\n- RED oracle: enter the real app lifespan through `TestClient` without any per-test background-task stubs and require a prompt successful health response; before the module fixture exists, the focused test is bounded by pytest-timeout and fails instead of inheriting a long shutdown.\n- Default path: the new autouse fixture makes the lifespan test prompt while the suite-wide environment value bounds shutdown.\n- Escape hatch: a `real_reconcile_loop`-marked lifespan test replaces only `reconcile_once` with a deterministic observable fake and proves the production `reconcile_loop` actually runs.\n- Override/control: the existing drain-specific test sets `SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS=0.1` and remains green; the stop-grace test continues to compute its floor from `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS`, pinning the production 1200-second constant.\n- Gates: focused pytest nodes first, then `make check` and `make test` using the worktree virtualenv; CI additionally exercises the required optional-extra lane.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every pytest test receives a small positive `SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS` baseline; verified by a root-conftest contract test and the focused review-bot tests.\n- [ ] The production default remains 1200 seconds; verified by the unchanged `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS` and the existing stop-grace-period test.\n- [ ] A test-local `SHUTDOWN_DRAIN_SECONDS=0.1` override wins over the suite baseline; verified by `test_lifespan_drain_is_bounded` remaining green.\n- [ ] Entering the review-bot lifespan is safe by default with no per-test reconciler/janitor stubs; verified by a new prompt TestClient health-path regression test.\n- [ ] The three duplicated reconciler/janitor setup sites are removed in favor of one module autouse fixture; verified by focused tests and review of the final diff.\n- [ ] A marked test explicitly runs the real production `reconcile_loop`; verified by an observable `reconcile_once` signal during lifespan startup.\n- [ ] The worktree passes `make check`, `make test`, Gerrit `LLM-Review +1`, and Gerrit `Verified +1` before submission."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786142756707283001,"uuid":"80141cb4-f190-45b5-9109-e994432e2660"}